{
  "about": "A device probe: the owner's run of the probe's own synthetic statements on one device, in `configure private`, never committed, every section ended with `rollback 0` and an empty `show | compare` at the end. Sanitized for this repository (docs/how-to/settle-a-schema-question.md, rule 5): no host name, user name, prompt or timestamp; the change-time attributes, the XML reply and CLI wrappers and the CLI banner are left out. `lines` are statements typed at the top level with the device's response: `accepted` is the load, `commit_check` the result of `commit check` where it ran. `edit_level` lines were typed at an edit level, which set input has no form for. `loads` are files loaded with `load`. `renderings` are `show` outputs, each with the configuration in the candidate when it was printed (`state`, as set lines) and what was asked (`show`). The questions and the backlog entries they settle are named by `id`. The raw session stays in private_test_data/device-probe-2026-10-16/.",
  "device": {
    "family": "QFX5120",
    "release": "25.2R2-S1.5",
    "date": "2026-10-16",
    "mode": "configure private; never committed"
  },
  "questions": {
    "D1": "HOLD-TIME-001: does `hold-time down 0` alone pass `commit check`?",
    "C3": "ANCESTOR-TAGS-001: how is a statement under a tagged ancestor printed?",
    "SC1": "RELATIVE-TAGS-001: does a bare `deactivate` or `protect` work at an edit level?",
    "A2": "LEAF-LIST-VALUE-TAGS-001: can one value of a leaf-list be tagged?",
    "D2": "RENAME-EVIDENCE-001: does the device load junoscfg's JSON names, and which does it print?",
    "D3": "JSON-KEYWORD-ALIAS-001: does the device load the CLI keyword in JSON?",
    "D4": "UNDOCUMENTED-001: undocumented siblings of modelled statements",
    "P4": "UNDOCUMENTED-001: `chassis dump-on-panic`",
    "D5": "VERB-PREFIX-001: a verb that stops before a list's name"
  },
